Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:40:38 +0300
Subject: Tux: spheres from cached vertex arrays, shadow in one draw
 (ETR_GL_TUX, ETR_GL_SHADOW)

gluSphere sent ~400 glNormal3f/glVertex3f calls in a dozen glBegin/glEnd pairs for each of 15 spheres in every frame. The same vertices (GLU's algorithm, floats) are made once per number of divisions as triangles in a buffer object. Nodes with the same material as the one before do not set it again.

The shadow's fans and strips went through glBegin/glNormal3d/glVertex3d per vertex (the normals unused, lighting is off); now the triangles of all spheres are collected and drawn at once.

diff --git a/src/tux.cpp b/src/tux.cpp
--- a/src/tux.cpp
+++ b/src/tux.cpp
@@ -30,8 +30,11 @@ still shaped with spheres.
